ink we collectively were  realizing what we were seeing  we said okay okay  we all thought it was her but we said we  got a call  i took my bag i had a string bag with me  and  opened it up to get a notebook out that  had detective grubs his phone number in  it but i've forgotten my notebook  i had my phone and my hand was shaking  the girl said it is an emergency if i  ever thought this was an emergency go  ahead and call 9-1-1  so i called 9-1-1  so florina she was very real and  emotional but what was the point of  calling her as a witness in that murder  case  um i think the only thing they wanted to  really get out of this is that the body  was not tampered with or touched because  remember the autopsy results are facial  fractures and neck fractures and that's  really important because the defense is  this is a suicide by a usb cord a usb  cord is not going to result in facial  fractures and a neck fracture and so the  only other possible defense or  explanation for those would be well  maybe whoever found her  stepped on her tampered with the body  did something to the body moved her and  caused those fractures and so while the  testimony itself doesn't seem  significant i believe the prosecution is  trying to close that door of explaining  away the fractures by having her be able  to say look we found her we called we  reported it we didn't touch the body we  didn't do anything in other words  there's no way they caused those  fractures  terry as we all know the prosecution has  the burden of proving the case beyond a  reasonable doubt how's the defense doing  raising doubts so far in the trial  oh i think that defense attorney has  done an excellent job so far starting  with the opening statement brian she  told that jury that she did not have to  present any evidence but guess what she  was going to anyway and one of the  witnesses that she  said she was going to call is an expert  who is testifying about the branch of  the tree and the fact that it could 